Leetcode Solved problems: Pattern Card

Problem Type     Pattern                      Keyline
Palindrome       process the digit            access every digit, create reverse number, compare.
Two Sum          Find pair that sums to x    | WHY: need O(1) lookup of complement
                                             | KEY LINE: complement = target - nums[i]
                                             |           if seen.count(complement) → found
                                             |           else seen[nums[i]] = i   
Longest prefix   Prefix reduction            Take whole string as prefix , then reduce the prefix after comparing 
string                                       with all strings accordingly. This is not sliding window as multiple strings are involved.

3 LONGEST COMMON PREFIX
Pattern  : Prefix reduction
Why      : Start with full first string, shrink until it fits all
Key line : while str.find(prefix) != 0 → prefix = prefix.substr(0, size-1)
Edge     : Empty array → ""

#4 MOVE ZEROES
Pattern  : Two pointers (slow/fast)
Why      : slow = where next non-zero goes, fast = scanner
Key line : if nums[fast] != 0 → swap(slow,fast) → slow++
           fast++ always (for loop)

5. Count unique occurrences : 
Pattern: Frequency map, hash map/set  
Why    : 1. Hash Map used to count frequency 
         2. hash set to check uniqueness of frequency.
KeyLine: mp[i]++; for every value in array.
         if st.count(freq) → return false
            else st.insert(freq)

