Learnings:
1. Two Sum:
- we use unordered container for two sum because its good for lookup.
- unordered containers dont use distance because they dont have meaningful indices.
- unordered_multiset - even if duplicates are allowed here, you cant access indices of these duplicates.
- So use unordered_map- doesnt take duplicates , but the keys are unique , so you know the proper index to access
- reserve space for unordered map.
- instead of insert pair(slower) use access specifier mp[nums[i]=i; 
- insert value as key because map searches with key.
